---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — SoloMD"
  description="SoloMD is a local-first Markdown editor that collects no personal data. Your notes never leave your device."
  lang="en"
>
  <main id="main" class="privacy">
    <article>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 2026-10-14</p>

      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <p>
        SoloMD is a local-first Markdown editor. <strong>Your notes never leave your device</strong>
        unless you send them somewhere yourself. The versions downloaded from our website and other
        stores send no usage data and no crash reports: there is no analytics endpoint behind the app,
        and nothing inside it that reports back. The only call it makes unprompted is the update check.
      </p>

      <h2>Data We Collect</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Nothing.</strong> SoloMD collects no usage data: no event counters, no device or
        install identifiers, no crash reports. There is no analytics endpoint behind the app and no
        analytics dependency inside it. That is true of every build, App Store included.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is no account system and no advertising, and nothing is shared with or sold to third
        parties.
      </p>

      <h2>Data You Create</h2>
      <p>
        All text, images, and files you create or open in SoloMD are stored locally on your device —
        inside the app's sandbox on iOS, or in folders you choose on macOS, Windows, and Linux.
        SoloMD does not upload this content to us.
      </p>
      <p>
        Features you set up yourself send what you choose directly to the service you chose: the AI
        provider you configure with your own key (or a local Ollama), GitHub / Gitea sync to your own
        repository, and an image host you configure. We never see that traffic.
      </p>

      <h2>Permissions We Request</h2>
      <p>SoloMD only uses system permissions required for its core editing function:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Local file access</strong> — to open, read, and save files you choose.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Photos library</strong> (only if you insert an image via the picker) — to read
          the single image you select.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not request contacts, location, microphone, camera, calendar, Bluetooth, or any
        other permission.
      </p>

      <h2>This Website</h2>
      <p>
        solomd.app sets no cookies, runs no third-party analytics, and keeps no visitor or download
        counters. There is no referral or campaign tracking either — nothing about your visit is
        sent anywhere, stored, or shared.
      </p>

      <h2>Third Parties</h2>
      <p>
        SoloMD does not embed any third-party analytics, advertising, crash reporting, or social
        media SDKs. The app's full source code is open at
        <a href="https://github.com/zhitongblog/solomd">github.com/zhitongblog/solomd</a> (MIT).
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        SoloMD is suitable for all ages and does not knowingly collect data from children.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        Any material changes will be reflected on this page and noted in the app's release notes.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions? Email <a href="mailto:slushy@139.com">slushy@139.com</a> or file an issue at
        <a href="https://github.com/zhitongblog/solomd/issues">github.com/zhitongblog/solomd/issues</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="lang-switch">
        <a href="/zh/privacy">中文版</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 1.5rem 6rem;
    color: var(--text, #1a1a1a);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .privacy h1 {
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.25em;
  }
  .privacy h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin: 2em 0 0.5em;
  }
  .privacy .updated {
    color: var(--text-muted, #777);
    margin: 0 0 2em;
  }
  .privacy a {
    color: var(--accent, #ff9f40);
  }
  .privacy ul {
    padding-left: 1.6em;
  }
  .lang-switch {
    margin-top: 3em;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
